{"summary":"The Cape crow or black crow (Corvus capensis) is slightly larger (48–50 cm in length) than the carrion crow and is completely black with a slight gloss of purple in its feathers. It has proportionately longer legs, wings and tail too and has a much longer, slimmer bill that seems to be adapted for probing into the ground for invertebrates. The head feathers have a coppery-purple gloss and the throat feathers are quite long and fluffed out...","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corvus capensis","cells":[[-19.0,12.3,1],[-19.6,15.8,2],[-19.0,14.4,2],[-19.0,15.1,1],[-19.0,17.2,2],[-19.0,15.8,3],[-19.0,16.5,3],[-19.6,25.0,1],[-20.3,24.3,1],[-21.0,23.6,1],[-20.3,25.0,1],[-21.6,23.6,1],[-19.0,24.3,1],[-21.0,25.7,1],[-20.3,23.6,1],[-20.3,26.4,1],[-24.2,16.5,1],[-25.5,15.8,1],[-28.6,17.2,1],[-33.4,19.3,1],[-30.4,18.6,1],[-29.2,18.6,1],[-29.2,17.2,1],[-28.0,17.2,1],[-33.4,18.6,1],[-30.4,17.9,2],[-22.9,15.8,1],[-27.4,16.5,1],[-26.1,16.5,1],[-32.8,19.3,1],[-22.9,14.4,2],[-24.8,22.1,1],[-24.8,20.0,1],[-26.7,15.1,1],[-26.7,15.8,1],[-24.8,15.8,2],[-26.7,16.5,2],[-34.0,20.0,3],[-24.2,15.8,2],[-24.8,15.1,2],[-30.4,17.2,1],[-25.5,16.5,1],[-22.9,15.1,2],[-33.4,20.0,1],[-24.8,20.7,1],[-22.3,14.4,1],[-26.1,15.8,1],[-25.5,20.7,2],[-33.4,22.1,2],[-29.2,17.9,1],[-23.6,15.8,2],[-34.6,19.3,2],[-22.3,17.2,1],[-31.7,18.6,1],[-34.0,21.4,2],[-26.1,20.0,2],[-23.6,15.1,2],[-31.1,19.3,2],[-31.7,20.0,1],[-34.0,20.7,2],[-26.7,20.7,2],[-29.2,16.5,1],[-29.8,17.2,2],[-34.0,22.1,2],[-33.4,20.7,2],[-26.1,20.7,3],[-34.6,20.0,3],[-31.7,19.3,2],[-34.0,19.3,2],[-33.4,21.4,2],[-25.5,20.0,2],[-34.6,20.7,2],[-32.8,25.7,1],[-31.7,29.2,1],[-28.6,32.0,1],[-21.6,23.6,1],[-28.6,23.6,1],[-25.5,29.2,1],[-28.6,31.3,1],[-27.4,29.2,1],[-28.0,30.6,1],[-26.7,29.2,1],[-25.5,27.1,1],[-28.0,29.2,1],[-30.4,28.5,1],[-26.1,30.6,1],[-32.2,27.1,1],[-31.7,28.5,1],[-30.4,27.1,1],[-26.7,27.1,1],[-32.8,27.1,2],[-26.1,31.3,1],[-31.1,29.9,1],[-24.8,22.1,1],[-34.0,26.4,2],[-26.1,25.7,1],[-24.8,29.9,1],[-25.5,29.9,2],[-27.4,